// Code only developers' tools or tests run.
//
// A dev or test build compiles more than the product: Mix tasks and the
// helpers they share, a project's test support, the test helpers a
// library ships in its own lib/, a development-only seed or dashboard.
// A defect there costs a developer's command or a test run, not the
// running system, and every analysis steps its finding down one level
// (Argus.Findings.Tooling, by the finding's module).
//
// tooling(mod, basis, permille): the module is tooling because its
// name or source path says so (`tooling_module`: basis "mix" or
// "test_support", permille 1000), or because the tooling prior is sure
// of it (basis "prior": the probability that it is a developer's tool
// or test support, at 0.9 or more; Argus.Priors.Questions.Tooling). The
// prior is asked only about modules the structure leaves undecided, and
// a module the prior is unsure of stays the product: the word errs
// quiet, toward the structural severity.
//
// A module the product calls into is not tooling, whatever its name or
// path: the deployed system runs it. akkoma's `pleroma_ctl` runs Mix
// tasks inside the live node (Pleroma.ReleaseTasks.run/1 calls
// Mix.Tasks.Pleroma.*.run/1), and an exam platform's `lib/exam/test/`
// is its Test context, which its controllers call. "Calls" is the call
// graph from a module that is not itself named tooling, and on through
// the named modules it reaches. Known limit: a call the graph does not
// resolve (akkoma finds the task module by name and applies it) leaves
// the module tooling.
//
// An analysis includes this file and declares `.output tooling`; its
// rows re-tier the analysis's findings and are no findings themselves.
// Requires imports.dl.

.decl tooling(mod: symbol, basis: symbol, permille: number)

tooling(m, basis, p) :- tooling_named(m, basis, p), !product_reached(m).

// What the structure or the prior names. 0.9 is where the calibration
// measured 8 of 9 re-tiers right over the modules holding a finding in
// the evaluation programs.
.decl tooling_named(mod: symbol, basis: symbol, permille: number)

tooling_named(m, basis, 1000) :- tooling_module(m, basis).

tooling_named(m, "prior", p) :-
  prior_tooling(m, _, _, p),
  p >= 900,
  !tooling_module(m, _).

.decl named_tooling(mod: symbol)

named_tooling(m) :- tooling_named(m, _, _).

// A named module a module of the product calls, or one such a module
// calls in turn.
.decl product_reached(mod: symbol)

product_reached(m) :-
  named_tooling(m),
  function_def(g, m, _, _, _),
  call_edge(c, g),
  function_def(c, cm, _, _, _),
  cm != m,
  !named_tooling(cm).

product_reached(m) :-
  product_reached(from),
  function_def(c, from, _, _, _),
  call_edge(c, g),
  function_def(g, m, _, _, _),
  m != from,
  named_tooling(m).
